Author: matiasrodriguezc01 <matiasrodriguezc01@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 15 22:53:14 2026 -0300

    Fix preload failing to load under Electron's default sandbox

    The compiled preload required '../shared/types' at runtime. Sandboxed preloads
    (the default since Electron 20) can only require 'electron', so the script threw
    'module not found' and window.knowledgeBase was never exposed: no IPC worked.

    Keep a local channel map typed as typeof IPC_CHANNELS via a type-only import,
    so the compiler still rejects any drift from src/shared/types.ts.

